1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,505
Finish your
coffee out here,

2
00:00:01,505 --> 00:00:03,735
and you’ll blister
by tonight.

3
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:05,580
The ozone
layer vanished

4
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:06,880
while you slept.

5
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,050
The sky looks
perfectly normal.

6
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:10,520
Ozone soaked
up the

7
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:12,320
harshest ultraviolet.

8
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:13,500
Now it burns
you about

9
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,070
thirty times
faster.

10
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:17,220
No sting,
no warning.

11
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:19,270
The burn shows
up hours later.

12
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,860
Shade only buys
you minutes.

13
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:24,120
The whole sky
scatters it.

14
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:24,760
Step inside,

15
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:27,240
and an ordinary
window saves you.

16
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:28,360
Glass stops
nearly

17
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:30,070
all the
burning rays.

18
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:32,380
Forget walking
anywhere.

19
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:33,760
A traffic
jam is now

20
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:35,570
the best seat
in town.

21
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:36,820
The same
sun that

22
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:38,240
burned you
is already

23
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:39,740
splitting
oxygen into

24
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:41,550
fresh ozone
overhead.

25
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:43,900
It takes weeks,
maybe months,

26
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:44,990
to refill.

27
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,020
Until then,

28
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:48,010
you watch daylight
through glass.

29
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:49,640
So you take
your coffee

30
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:51,720
outside
after dark.

31
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:54,110
Nightfall becomes
your morning.
